Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Meshing: the polygons of two consecutive edges of a face's wire that leave
their common vertex in nearly the same direction in the face's parameter
plane (a cusp of the wire) and cross each other near it are untangled
before the face is meshed, so that the face gets its triangles
(mitcad#2022).

The corner plates of fillets (ChFi3d's PerformMoreThreeCorner) pinch to a
point where they meet a sharp edge or a stripe's end on a contact going on
tangentially: their wires have corners of almost no angle (0.2 to 0.5
degrees in the plate's parameter plane). On the reported bent guide of
mitcad#2009, at a deviation of 0.002 with an angle of 2 or 5 degrees, the
polygon of the stripe's end section, finely divided, crossed the first,
long segment of the polygon of the plate's border along the rim near such
a corner: a loop far smaller than the face checker's threshold (a circle
twice the face's deflection across, which the plate's tolerances make
0.1 and more), so it was left as it was, and the Delaunay triangulation
of a frontier crossing itself had no inside: "a face could not be
triangulated" (BRepMesh_BaseMeshAlgo::commitSurfaceTriangulation).

- BRepMesh_ModelHealer::performInternal, before the faces are checked,
  and amplifyEdges, before the faces of amplified edges are checked again:
  untangleCusps, one face after another. For each two consecutive edges
  of a wire with a common vertex whose first segments from it lie within 5
  degrees of each other, while a segment of one polygon crosses a segment
  of the other (not the two first ones), the point next to the vertex is
  taken out of one polygon: the one whose crossing segment is fewer
  segments from the vertex, unless that segment is its first one, then the
  other. It is taken out of the edge's curve and all its pcurves, so that
  the faces sharing the edge keep one polygon; at last the polygon's first
  segment goes from the vertex past the crossing.
- Elsewhere nothing changes. No catch is added.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 1804.

